<title>INDIA: Indian union leader shot dead-news agency.</title>
<headline>Indian union leader shot dead-news agency.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian trade union leader Datta Samant was shot dead by unidentified gunmen on Thursday, the Press Trust of India news agency said.  </p>
<p>Police officials would not confirm he was dead.</p>
<p>&quot;He was fired upon. We have no other details,&quot; one official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The PTI newsagency said Samant was shot by autorickshaw-borne assailants while he was travelling in his car. &quot;Samant was immediately rushed to hospital ....but succumbed to bullet injuries,&quot; PTI said.</p>
</text>
